&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;International Accounting Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to oversee global accounting operations and support the company&#39;s expanding international footprint. This role will lead multi-entity global consolidations, ensure accurate intercompany accounting and eliminations across multiple international jurisdictions, and partner closely with local finance teams and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver timely financial reporting, regulatory compliance, and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Accounting &amp;amp; Consolidations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead monthly, quarterly, and annual multi-entity global consolidations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate intercompany accounting, reconciliations, and eliminations across global subsidiaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and analyze consolidated financial statements and supporting schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage foreign currency translation, consolidation adjustments, and CTA accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of cross-border transactions and intercompany balances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the global month-end and year-end close processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Entity Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accounting operations and statutory compliance across entities in the United States, Canada, Bahamas, United Kingdom, Japan, Spain, Singapore, India, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA), and United Arab Emirates (UAE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with local accounting firms, auditors, tax advisors, and consultants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional finance teams to ensure timely month-end close and financial reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with U.S. GAAP, IFRS, and applicable local accounting standards and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Reporting &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, and variance analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits across global entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in preparing statutory financial statements and regulatory filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and strengthen internal controls, accounting policies, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate and improve international accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ERP implementations, migrations, and financial systems optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance consolidation, reporting, and close processes to improve scalability and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop standardized accounting procedures across international entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Tax, Treasury, FP&amp;amp;A, Payroll, Legal, Operations, and People teams on international business initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support global expansion efforts, including new entity setup, acquisitions, and operational integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide accounting guidance on international transactions, entity structures, and business initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA or equivalent professional accounting certification preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–10+ years of progressive accounting experience, including significant international accounting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in multi-entity consolidations and intercompany accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting accounting operations across multiple global jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough knowledge of U.S. GAAP; IFRS experience strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise ERP systems (e.g., NetSuite, Oracle, SAP, Workday Financials)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills and strong financial reporting capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, organizational, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, high-growth global environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public accounting experience (Big Four or national firm preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, financial services, SaaS, or other high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with statutory reporting requirements across North America, EMEA, and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP implementations, accounting system migrations, or finance transformation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with consolidation software (e.g., OneStream, BlackLine, FloQast, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of SOX controls and internal control frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting international expansion and new legal entity launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
